Z||000000||Fiero Justin||02-11-2001||12:55 PM||||Ok here is my problem:  <BR>Since I bought my 86 SE in July, the two most exterior tail lights on both sides intermittantly stay on when all lights and the car are turned off.  The only way that I can turn them off is to pull the stop light fuse.  My third brake light doesn't stay on either.  Any replies would help, being that this is my only car to drive.||||reg||4
Z||000001||MrPBody||02-11-2001||04:52 PM||||Are those your brake lights?  Could be a stuck or maladjusted brake light switch.  Just guessing.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||02-11-2001||05:23 PM||||Not sure how the 86's are wired, but my 84 SE has a pair of relays in the engine compartment that control only the very outboard stoplight bulbs. 1 relay for the left and 1 for the right.  I had a problem once with the right hand relay sticking and leaving the outside r/h stoplight lit.  I tossed in a spare relay I had laying around and solved the problem.  Seems like a strange set up to me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
